{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VYE7128szrCpyPgSm3S6vX","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t//! Translation of `quic/binlog.h`.\n2\t//!\n3\t//! Public surface of the binary trace (\"binlog\") backend.  The\n4\t//! header exposes two flavours of entry point:\n5\t//!\n6\t//! 1. **Top-level wiring** ([`Quic::set_binlog`],\n7\t//!    [`Quic::enable_binlog`]) that installs the binlog vtable on a\n8\t//!    QUIC context.  `binlog_dir == NULL` in C is the \"stop tracing\"\n9\t//!    sentinel; [`Quic::enable_binlog`] only flips the vtable\n10\t//!    pointer and is used when autoqlog wants the binary stream\n11\t//!    without a dedicated directory.\n12\t//! 2. **Per-event writers** that emit one trace record.  In C they\n13\t//!    all bottom out in `fwrite()` against either an out-of-band\n14\t//!    `FILE*` or `connection->f_binlog` pulled from the connection.  The\n15\t//!    Rust split mirrors that: the three file-only writers ([`pdu`],\n16\t//!    [`packet`], [`tls_ticket`]) are free functions on a [`File`]\n17\t//!    sink, and the rest hang on the [`Binlog`] trait implemented for\n18\t//!    [`Connection`] (they pull the file handle from\n19\t//!    `connection.f_binlog` themselves).\n20\t//!\n21\t//! Pointer-shape and translation policy notes for this module:\n22\t//!\n23\t//! * `FILE*` (the three low-level writers) → `&mut std::fs::File`.\n24\t//!   These calls borrow the handle for the duration of one record\n25\t//!   write — ownership stays with the connection (`connection->f_binlog`)\n26\t//!   or the caller.  The binlog stream is *binary*, so the text-side\n27\t//!   `&mut impl core::fmt::Write` convention used by\n28\t//!   [`crate::textlog`] does not apply here.\n29\t//! * `Quic*` / `Connection*` — every observed caller passes a non-NULL\n30\t//!   handle and the body mutates internal state (`quic->bin_log_fns`,\n31\t//!   `connection->f_binlog`, `quic->binlog_dir`).  Free functions\n32\t//!   keyed on `Quic*` become inherent methods on [`Quic`]; those keyed\n33\t//!   on `Connection*` become methods on the [`Binlog`] trait\n34\t//!   (implemented for [`Connection`]).\n35\t//! * `Path*` — only ever accessed inside\n36\t//!   `binlog_get_path_id(connection, path_x)`, which dereferences `path_x`\n37\t//!   to read `unique_path_id`.  Every observed caller passes a\n38\t//!   non-NULL path handle, so this is `&mut Path` for parity with\n39\t//!   the unified-log dispatch trait (which takes the path mutably\n40\t//!   for the same hooks).\n41\t//! * `const ConnectionId*` (in [`pdu`] / [`packet`]) →\n42\t//!   `&ConnectionId`.  The C contract is \"must be non-NULL\"; every\n43\t//!   caller passes `&connection->initial_connection_id`.\n44\t//! * `ConnectionId* dcid` (in [`Binlog::packet_lost`]) is\n45\t//!   nullable per `loss_recovery.c` — when no remote CID is known\n46\t//!   the C call site passes NULL and the body emits a single zero\n47\t//!   length byte.  Maps to `Option<&ConnectionId>`.  The C signature\n48\t//!   drops `const` but the body only reads through the pointer, so\n49\t//!   the Rust equivalent stays a shared borrow.\n50\t//! * `packet_header* ph` (in [`Binlog::dropped_packet`],\n51\t//!   [`Binlog::outgoing_packet`]) — the body only *reads*\n52\t//!   `ph->ptype` in the dropped path and reconstructs a fresh header\n53\t//!   in the outgoing path.  In [`Binlog::outgoing_packet`] the\n54\t//!   parsed-header buffer is constructed locally, so no pointer\n55\t//!   crosses the API boundary.  In [`packet`] /\n56\t//!   [`Binlog::dropped_packet`] we map `ph` to `&PacketHeader`\n57\t//!   (immutable borrow) — matching the unified-log trait shape.\n58\t//! * `ConnectionId connection_id` (in [`tls_ticket`]) is `Copy` and\n59\t//!   pass-by-value, mirroring the C ABI.\n60\t//! * `const struct sockaddr*` pairs (`addr_peer`, `addr_local` in\n61\t//!   [`pdu`]) → `&core::net::SocketAddr`, matching the convention\n62\t//!   established in [`crate::logger`].\n63\t//! * `const uint8_t* + size_t` argument pairs collapse to `&[u8]`\n64\t//!   (`bytes`/`bytes_max` in [`packet`], `params`/`param_length` in\n65\t//!   [`Binlog::transport_extension`], `ticket`/`ticket_length`\n66\t//!   in [`tls_ticket`], `sni`/`sni_len` and `alpn`/`alpn_len` in\n67\t//!   [`Binlog::negotiated_alpn`]).  An empty slice models the C\n68\t//!   `(NULL, 0)` callers cleanly.\n69\t//! * [`Binlog::outgoing_packet`] carries *two* buffers: the\n70\t//!   unencrypted `bytes` (length passed separately as `length`) and\n71\t//!   the encrypted `send_buffer` (length passed separately as\n72\t//!   `send_length`).  Each pair collapses to one `&[u8]`.  The\n73\t//!   `pn_length` parameter — the offset of the packet-number field\n74\t//!   inside `bytes` — survives as a separate `usize`.\n75\t//! * `const PtlsIovec* alpn_list, size_t alpn_count` →\n76\t//!   `&[&[u8]]`, mirroring the unified-log trait shape.\n77\t//! * `int receiving` / `int is_local` are pure 0/1 flags promoted to\n78\t//!   `bool`; `int err` is a real signed status code so it stays\n79\t//!   `i32`.\n80\t//! * `unsigned char ecn` collapses to `u8`.\n81\t//! * `char const* binlog_dir` is the C \"stop tracing when NULL\"\n82\t//!   sentinel, so [`Quic::set_binlog`] takes `Option<&str>`.\n83\t//!   `Some(path)` installs the vtable and copies the directory name\n84\t//!   into the QUIC context; `None` leaves the directory cleared\n85\t//!   while still wiring up the vtable.\n86\t//! * `char const* trigger` (in [`Binlog::packet_lost`]) is\n87\t//!   always a non-NULL static string literal at the call sites\n88\t//!   grepped in `loss_recovery.c`, so it maps to `&str`.\n89\t//!\n90\t//! Error handling: [`Quic::set_binlog`] mirrors the C `int` return\n91\t//! (always `0` today, but reserved for future failure modes) as\n92\t//! `Result<(), Error>` per the project's error-handling convention.\n93\t\n94\tuse std::fs::File;\n95\tuse std::io::Write;\n96\tuse std::path::{Path as FsPath, PathBuf};\n97\t\n98\tuse core::net::SocketAddr;\n99\t\n100\tuse crate::Error;\n101\tuse crate::Instant;\n102\tuse crate::bytestream::{BYTESTREAM_MAX_BUFFER_SIZE, ByteStream, ByteStreamBuf};\n103\tuse crate::frames::FrameType;\n104\tuse crate::internal::{\n105\t    Connection, PacketHeader, PacketType, Path, frames_varint_decode, frames_varint_skip,\n106\t    varint_decode, varint_encode,\n107\t};\n108\tuse crate::{ConnectionId, Quic};\n109\t\n110\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n111\t// Event-tag enum.\n112\t//\n113\t// The C `picoquic_log_event_type` is a sparse enum with explicit\n114\t// hex constants — the values are baked into the binary log format\n115\t// and must round-trip through the wire untouched.  Translated as a\n116\t// Rust enum with `#[repr(u32)]` so each variant keeps its\n117\t// wire-format tag; `repr(C)` is *not* used because the type does\n118\t// not cross an FFI boundary — the discriminant is only serialized\n119\t// as a varint by `binlog_compose_event_header`.\n120\t\n121\t/// Event tag emitted at the start of every binary log record.  The\n122\t/// underlying integer values are part of the binlog wire format and\n123\t/// must not drift from the C enum.\n124\t#[repr(u32)]\n125\t#[derive(Debug, Copy, Clone, PartialEq, Eq)]\n126\tpub enum LogEventType {\n127\t    PduSent = 0x0002,\n128\t    PduRecv = 0x0003,\n129\t\n130\t    PacketSent = 0x0008,\n131\t    PacketRecv = 0x0009,\n132\t\n133\t    NewConnection = 0x0010,\n134\t    ConnectionClose = 0x0011,\n135\t    ConnectionIdUpdate = 0x0012,\n136\t    PacketLost = 0x0013,\n137\t    PacketDropped = 0x0014,\n138\t    PacketBuffered = 0x0015,\n139\t\n140\t    TlsKeyUpdate = 0x0020,\n141\t    TlsKeyRetired = 0x0021,\n142\t\n143\t    VersionUpdate = 0x0035,\n144\t    ParamUpdate = 0x0036,\n145\t    AlpnUpdate = 0x0037,\n146\t    CcUpdate = 0x0038,\n147\t    StreamUpdate = 0x0039,\n148\t    InfoMessage = 0x003a,\n149\t\n150\t    FrameSent = 0x0082,\n151\t    FrameRecv = 0x0083,\n152\t}\n153\t\n154\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n155\t// Helpers private to this module.\n156\t\n157\t/// Big-endian 4-byte length prefix + payload.  C: the trailing\n158\t/// `fwrite(head, 4, …); fwrite(data, len, …)` pair that every\n159\t/// binlog record ends with.\n160\tfn write_record(f: &mut File, payload: &[u8]) {\n161\t    let head = (payload.len() as u32).to_be_bytes();\n162\t    let _ = f.write_all(&head);\n163\t    let _ = f.write_all(payload);\n164\t}\n165\t\n166\t/// Write the per-record common prefix.  C: `binlog_compose_event_header`.\n167\tfn compose_event_header(\n168\t    msg: &mut ByteStream<'_>,\n169\t    cid: &ConnectionId,\n170\t    current_time: Instant,\n171\t    path_id: u64,\n172\t    event_type: LogEventType,\n173\t) {\n174\t    let _ = msg.write_cid(cid);\n175\t    let _ = msg.write_varint(current_time.ticks());\n176\t    let _ = msg.write_varint(path_id);\n177\t    let _ = msg.write_varint(event_type as u64);\n178\t}\n179\t\n180\t/// C: `binlog_get_path_id`.\n181\tfn get_path_id(connection: &Connection, path_x: &Path) -> u64 {\n182\t    if connection.is_multipath_enabled {\n183\t        path_x.unique_path_id\n184\t    } else {\n185\t        0\n186\t    }\n187\t}\n188\t\n189\t/// Append a varint-encoded `value` to `out`.\n190\tfn append_varint(out: &mut Vec<u8>, value: u64) {\n191\t    let mut buf = [0u8; 8];\n192\t    let n = varint_encode(&mut buf, value);\n193\t    out.extend_from_slice(&buf[..n]);\n194\t}\n195\t\n196\t/// Append a length-prefixed copy of `frame_bytes` to `out`.\n197\t/// C: `picoquic_binlog_frame`.\n198\tfn append_frame(out: &mut Vec<u8>, frame_bytes: &[u8]) {\n199\t    append_varint(out, frame_bytes.len() as u64);\n200\t    out.extend_from_slice(frame_bytes);\n201\t}\n202\t\n203\t/// Minimal packet-header parser sufficient for binlog's outgoing-packet\n204\t/// record.  C: `picoquic_parse_packet_header` populates a richer\n205\t/// `PacketHeader`, but reaches into `Quic` for the version table; the\n206\t/// trait method [`Binlog::outgoing_packet`] runs without a Quic\n207\t/// back-pointer, so we only extract what the binlog wire format\n208\t/// actually serializes (type, version, CIDs, header offsets).\n209\tfn parse_outgoing_header(send_buffer: &[u8]) -> PacketHeader {\n210\t    let mut ph = PacketHeader::default();\n211\t    if send_buffer.is_empty() {\n212\t        ph.packet_type = PacketType::Error;\n213\t        return ph;\n214\t    }\n215\t    let flags = send_buffer[0];\n216\t    if flags & 0x80 == 0 {\n217\t        // Short header — only 1-RTT in flight.\n218\t        ph.packet_type = PacketType::OneRttProtected;\n219\t        ph.spin = (flags & 0x20) != 0;\n220\t        ph.key_phase = (flags & 0x04) != 0;\n221\t        ph.quic_bit_is_zero = (flags & 0x40) == 0;\n222\t        ph.offset = 1; // CIDs are not on the short-header wire.\n223\t        ph.payload_length_value = send_buffer.len().saturating_sub(1);\n224\t        ph.payload_length = ph.payload_length_value;\n225\t        ph.packet_number_offset = 1;\n226\t        return ph;\n227\t    }\n228\t\n229\t    if send_buffer.len() < 5 {\n230\t        ph.packet_type = PacketType::Error;\n231\t        return ph;\n232\t    }\n233\t    let version = u32::from_be_bytes([\n234\t        send_buffer[1],\n235\t        send_buffer[2],\n236\t        send_buffer[3],\n237\t        send_buffer[4],\n238\t    ]);\n239\t    ph.version = version;\n240\t    let mut pos = 5usize;\n241\t\n242\t    if pos >= send_buffer.len() {\n243\t        ph.packet_type = PacketType::Error;\n244\t        return ph;\n245\t    }\n246\t    let dcid_len = send_buffer[pos] as usize;\n247\t    pos += 1;\n248\t    if pos + dcid_len > send_buffer.len() {\n249\t        ph.packet_type = PacketType::Error;\n250\t        return ph;\n251\t    }\n252\t    if let Some(cid) = ConnectionId::clone_from_slice(&send_buffer[pos..pos + dcid_len]) {\n253\t        ph.dest_connection_id = cid;\n254\t    }\n255\t    pos += dcid_len;\n256\t\n257\t    if pos >= send_buffer.len() {\n258\t        ph.packet_type = PacketType::Error;\n259\t        return ph;\n260\t    }\n261\t    let scid_len = send_buffer[pos] as usize;\n262\t    pos += 1;\n263\t    if pos + scid_len > send_buffer.len() {\n264\t        ph.packet_type = PacketType::Error;\n265\t        return ph;\n266\t    }\n267\t    if let Some(cid) = ConnectionId::clone_from_slice(&send_buffer[pos..pos + scid_len]) {\n268\t        ph.src_connection_id = cid;\n269\t    }\n270\t    pos += scid_len;\n271\t\n272\t    if version == 0 {\n273\t        ph.packet_type = PacketType::VersionNegotiation;\n274\t        ph.offset = pos;\n275\t        ph.payload_length_value = send_buffer.len().saturating_sub(pos);\n276\t        ph.payload_length = ph.payload_length_value;\n277\t        return ph;\n278\t    }\n279\t\n280\t    ph.packet_type = crate::internal::parse_long_packet_type(flags, 0);\n281\t    ph.quic_bit_is_zero = (flags & 0x40) == 0;\n282\t\n283\t    if ph.packet_type == PacketType::Initial {\n284\t        let mut tok_len = 0u64;\n285\t        match frames_varint_decode(&send_buffer[pos..], &mut tok_len) {\n286\t            Some(rest) => {\n287\t                pos = send_buffer.len() - rest.len();\n288\t                let token_end = pos.saturating_add(tok_len as usize);\n289\t                if token_end <= send_buffer.len() {\n290\t                    ph.token_bytes = send_buffer[pos..token_end].to_vec();\n291\t                    pos = token_end;\n292\t                }\n293\t            }\n294\t            None => {\n295\t                ph.packet_type = PacketType::Error;\n296\t                return ph;\n297\t            }\n298\t        }\n299\t    }\n300\t\n301\t    if ph.packet_type == PacketType::Retry {\n302\t        ph.offset = pos;\n303\t        ph.payload_length_value = send_buffer.len().saturating_sub(pos);\n304\t        ph.payload_length = ph.payload_length_value;\n305\t        return ph;\n306\t    }\n307\t\n308\t    // Long-header payload-length varint, then PN.\n309\t    let mut payload_len = 0u64;\n310\t    let after_len = match frames_varint_decode(&send_buffer[pos..], &mut payload_len) {\n311\t        Some(r) => r,\n312\t        None => {\n313\t            ph.packet_type = PacketType::Error;\n314\t            return ph;\n315\t        }\n316\t    };\n317\t    let len_consumed = (send_buffer.len() - after_len.len()) - pos;\n318\t    pos += len_consumed;\n319\t    ph.packet_number_offset = pos;\n320\t    ph.offset = pos;\n321\t    ph.payload_length_value = payload_len as usize;\n322\t    ph.payload_length = payload_len as usize;\n323\t\n324\t    ph\n325\t}\n326\t\n327\t// Frame parsers used by `binlog_frames`.\n328\t\n329\tfn skip_fixed(bytes: &[u8], size: usize) -> Option<&[u8]> {\n330\t    bytes.get(size..)\n331\t}\n332\t\n333\tfn read_length(bytes: &[u8]) -> Option<(usize, &[u8])> {\n334\t    let mut n64 = 0u64;\n335\t    let rest = frames_varint_decode(bytes, &mut n64)?;\n336\t    let n = n64 as usize;\n337\t    if (n as u64) != n64 {\n338\t        return None;\n339\t    }\n340\t    Some((n, rest))\n341\t}\n342\t\n343\tfn log_stream_frame<'a>(out: &mut Vec<u8>, bytes_in: &'a [u8]) -> Option<&'a [u8]> {\n344\t    let bytes_begin = bytes_in;\n345\t    if bytes_in.is_empty() {\n346\t        return None;\n347\t    }\n348\t    let ftype = bytes_in[0];\n349\t    let mut bytes = skip_fixed(bytes_in, 1)?;\n350\t    bytes = frames_varint_skip(bytes)?;\n351\t    if (ftype & 4) != 0 {\n352\t        bytes = frames_varint_skip(bytes)?;\n353\t    }\n354\t\n355\t    let head_len = bytes_begin.len() - bytes.len();\n356\t    let has_length = (ftype & 2) != 0;\n357\t    let length: usize;\n358\t    if has_length {\n359\t        let (l, rest) = read_length(bytes)?;\n360\t        length = l;\n361\t        bytes = rest;\n362\t    } else {\n363\t        length = bytes.len();\n364\t    }\n365\t\n366\t    let mut extra_bytes: usize = 8;\n367\t    if length < extra_bytes {\n368\t        extra_bytes = length;\n369\t    }\n370\t\n371\t    if has_length {\n372\t        let copy_end = head_len.saturating_add(extra_bytes).min(bytes_begin.len());\n373\t        append_frame(out, &bytes_begin[..copy_end]);\n374\t    } else {\n375\t        let mut log_buffer = Vec::with_capacity(head_len + 8 + extra_bytes);\n376\t        log_buffer.extend_from_slice(&bytes_begin[..head_len]);\n377\t        let mut len_buf = [0u8; 8];\n378\t        let n = varint_encode(&mut len_buf, length as u64);\n379\t        log_buffer.extend_from_slice(&len_buf[..n]);\n380\t        let payload_start = head_len;\n381\t        let avail = bytes_begin.len().saturating_sub(payload_start);\n382\t        let take = extra_bytes.min(avail);\n383\t        log_buffer.extend_from_slice(&bytes_begin[payload_start..payload_start + take]);\n384\t        append_frame(out, &log_buffer);\n385\t    }\n386\t\n387\t    skip_fixed(bytes, length)\n388\t}\n389\t\n390\tfn log_ack_frame<'a>(out: &mut Vec<u8>, bytes_in: &'a [u8]) -> Option<&'a [u8]> {\n391\t    let bytes_begin = bytes_in;\n392\t    let mut ftype = 0u64;\n393\t    let _ = frames_varint_decode(bytes_in, &mut ftype)?;\n394\t    let mut bytes = frames_varint_skip(bytes_in)?;\n395\t    if ftype == FrameType::PathAck as u64 || ftype == FrameType::PathAckEcn as u64 {\n396\t        bytes = frames_varint_skip(bytes)?;\n397\t    }\n398\t    bytes = frames_varint_skip(bytes)?;\n399\t    bytes = frames_varint_skip(bytes)?;\n400\t    let mut nb_blocks = 0u64;\n401\t    bytes = frames_varint_decode(bytes, &mut nb_blocks)?;\n402\t    bytes = frames_varint_skip(bytes)?;\n403\t    for _ in 0..nb_blocks {\n404\t        bytes = frames_varint_skip(bytes)?;\n405\t        bytes = frames_varint_skip(bytes)?;\n406\t    }\n407\t    if ftype == FrameType::AckEcn as u64 || ftype == FrameType::PathAckEcn as u64 {\n408\t        bytes = frames_varint_skip(bytes)?;\n409\t        bytes = frames_varint_skip(bytes)?;\n410\t        bytes = frames_varint_skip(bytes)?;\n411\t    }\n412\t    let consumed = bytes_begin.len() - bytes.len();\n413\t    append_frame(out, &bytes_begin[..consumed]);\n414\t    Some(bytes)\n415\t}\n416\t\n417\tfn log_simple_n_varints<'a>(\n418\t    out: &mut Vec<u8>,\n419\t    bytes_in: &'a [u8],\n420\t    skip_byte: bool,\n421\t    n: usize,\n422\t) -> Option<&'a [u8]> {\n423\t    let bytes_begin = bytes_in;\n424\t    let mut bytes = if skip_byte {\n425\t        skip_fixed(bytes_in, 1)?\n426\t    } else {\n427\t        frames_varint_skip(bytes_in)?\n428\t    };\n429\t    for _ in 0..n {\n430\t        bytes = frames_varint_skip(bytes)?;\n431\t    }\n432\t    let consumed = bytes_begin.len() - bytes.len();\n433\t    append_frame(out, &bytes_begin[..consumed]);\n434\t    Some(bytes)\n435\t}\n436\t\n437\tfn log_close_frame<'a>(out: &mut Vec<u8>, bytes_in: &'a [u8]) -> Option<&'a [u8]> {\n438\t    let bytes_begin = bytes_in;\n439\t    let mut bytes = skip_fixed(bytes_in, 1)?;\n440\t    bytes = frames_varint_skip(bytes)?;\n441\t    bytes = frames_varint_skip(bytes)?;\n442\t    let (length, rest) = read_length(bytes)?;\n443\t    bytes = skip_fixed(rest, length)?;\n444\t    let consumed = bytes_begin.len() - bytes.len();\n445\t    append_frame(out, &bytes_begin[..consumed]);\n446\t    Some(bytes)\n447\t}\n448\t\n449\tfn log_app_close_frame<'a>(out: &mut Vec<u8>, bytes_in: &'a [u8]) -> Option<&'a [u8]> {\n450\t    let bytes_begin = bytes_in;\n451\t    let mut bytes = skip_fixed(bytes_in, 1)?;\n452\t    bytes = frames_varint_skip(bytes)?;\n453\t    let (length, rest) = read_length(bytes)?;\n454\t    bytes = skip_fixed(rest, length)?;\n455\t    let consumed = bytes_begin.len() - bytes.len();\n456\t    append_frame(out, &bytes_begin[..consumed]);\n457\t    Some(bytes)\n458\t}\n459\t\n460\tfn log_new_connection_id_frame<'a>(out: &mut Vec<u8>, bytes_in: &'a [u8]) -> Option<&'a [u8]> {\n461\t    let bytes_begin = bytes_in;\n462\t    let mut bytes = skip_fixed(bytes_in, 1)?;\n463\t    bytes = frames_varint_skip(bytes)?;\n464\t    bytes = frames_varint_skip(bytes)?;\n465\t    if bytes.is_empty() {\n466\t        return None;\n467\t    }\n468\t    let cid_len = bytes[0] as usize;\n469\t    bytes = skip_fixed(bytes, 1 + cid_len)?;\n470\t    bytes = skip_fixed(bytes, crate::RESET_SECRET_SIZE)?;\n471\t    let consumed = bytes_begin.len() - bytes.len();\n472\t    append_frame(out, &bytes_begin[..consumed]);\n473\t    Some(bytes)\n474\t}\n475\t\n476\tfn log_path_new_connection_id_frame<'a>(out: &mut Vec<u8>, bytes_in: &'a [u8]) -> Option<&'a [u8]> {\n477\t    let bytes_begin = bytes_in;\n478\t    let mut bytes = frames_varint_skip(bytes_in)?;\n479\t    bytes = frames_varint_skip(bytes)?;\n480\t    bytes = frames_varint_skip(bytes)?;\n481\t    bytes = frames_varint_skip(bytes)?;\n482\t    if bytes.is_empty() {\n483\t        return None;\n484\t    }\n485\t    let cid_len = bytes[0] as usize;\n486\t    bytes = skip_fixed(bytes, 1 + cid_len)?;\n487\t    bytes = skip_fixed(bytes, crate::RESET_SECRET_SIZE)?;\n488\t    let consumed = bytes_begin.len() - bytes.len();\n489\t    append_frame(out, &bytes_begin[..consumed]);\n490\t    Some(bytes)\n491\t}\n492\t\n493\tfn log_new_token_frame<'a>(out: &mut Vec<u8>, bytes_in: &'a [u8]) -> Option<&'a [u8]> {\n494\t    let bytes_begin = bytes_in;\n495\t    let mut bytes = skip_fixed(bytes_in, 1)?;\n496\t    let (length, rest) = read_length(bytes)?;\n497\t    bytes = skip_fixed(rest, length)?;\n498\t    let consumed = bytes_begin.len() - bytes.len();\n499\t    append_frame(out, &bytes_begin[..consumed]);\n500\t    Some(bytes)\n501\t}\n502\t\n503\tfn log_path_frame<'a>(out: &mut Vec<u8>, bytes_in: &'a [u8]) -> Option<&'a [u8]> {\n504\t    let bytes = skip_fixed(bytes_in, 1 + 8)?;\n505\t    let consumed = bytes_in.len() - bytes.len();\n506\t    append_frame(out, &bytes_in[..consumed]);\n507\t    Some(bytes)\n508\t}\n509\t\n510\tfn log_crypto_hs_frame<'a>(out: &mut Vec<u8>, bytes_in: &'a [u8]) -> Option<&'a [u8]> {\n511\t    let bytes_begin = bytes_in;\n512\t    let mut bytes = skip_fixed(bytes_in, 1)?;\n513\t    bytes = frames_varint_skip(bytes)?;\n514\t    let (length, rest) = read_length(bytes)?;\n515\t    bytes = rest;\n516\t    let header_len = bytes_begin.len() - bytes.len();\n517\t    append_frame(out, &bytes_begin[..header_len]);\n518\t    bytes = skip_fixed(bytes, length)?;\n519\t    Some(bytes)\n520\t}\n521\t\n522\tfn log_handshake_done_frame<'a>(out: &mut Vec<u8>, bytes_in: &'a [u8]) -> Option<&'a [u8]> {\n523\t    let bytes = skip_fixed(bytes_in, 1)?;\n524\t    let consumed = bytes_in.len() - bytes.len();\n525\t    append_frame(out, &bytes_in[..consumed]);\n526\t    Some(bytes)\n527\t}\n528\t\n529\tfn log_datagram_frame<'a>(out: &mut Vec<u8>, bytes_in: &'a [u8]) -> Option<&'a [u8]> {\n530\t    let bytes_begin = bytes_in;\n531\t    if bytes_in.is_empty() {\n532\t        return None;\n533\t    }\n534\t    let ftype = bytes_in[0];\n535\t    let mut bytes = skip_fixed(bytes_in, 1)?;\n536\t    let length: usize;\n537\t    if ftype & 1 != 0 {\n538\t        let (l, rest) = read_length(bytes)?;\n539\t        length = l;\n540\t        bytes = rest;\n541\t    } else {\n542\t        length = bytes.len();\n543\t    }\n544\t    let header_len = bytes_begin.len() - bytes.len();\n545\t    append_frame(out, &bytes_begin[..header_len]);\n546\t    bytes = skip_fixed(bytes, length)?;\n547\t    Some(bytes)\n548\t}\n549\t\n550\tfn log_time_stamp_frame<'a>(out: &mut Vec<u8>, bytes_in: &'a [u8]) -> Option<&'a [u8]> {\n551\t    let bytes_begin = bytes_in;\n552\t    let mut bytes = frames_varint_skip(bytes_in)?;\n553\t    bytes = frames_varint_skip(bytes)?;\n554\t    let consumed = bytes_begin.len() - bytes.len();\n555\t    append_frame(out, &bytes_begin[..consumed]);\n556\t    Some(bytes)\n557\t}\n558\t\n559\tfn log_path_abandon_frame<'a>(out: &mut Vec<u8>, bytes_in: &'a [u8]) -> Option<&'a [u8]> {\n560\t    let bytes_begin = bytes_in;\n561\t    let mut bytes = frames_varint_skip(bytes_in)?;\n562\t    bytes = frames_varint_skip(bytes)?;\n563\t    bytes = frames_varint_skip(bytes)?;\n564\t    let consumed = bytes_begin.len() - bytes.len();\n565\t    append_frame(out, &bytes_begin[..consumed]);\n566\t    Some(bytes)\n567\t}\n568\t\n569\tfn log_path_available_or_backup_frame<'a>(\n570\t    out: &mut Vec<u8>,\n571\t    bytes_in: &'a [u8],\n572\t) -> Option<&'a [u8]> {\n573\t    let bytes_begin = bytes_in;\n574\t    let mut bytes = frames_varint_skip(bytes_in)?;\n575\t    bytes = frames_varint_skip(bytes)?;\n576\t    bytes = frames_varint_skip(bytes)?;\n577\t    let consumed = bytes_begin.len() - bytes.len();\n578\t    append_frame(out, &bytes_begin[..consumed]);\n579\t    Some(bytes)\n580\t}\n581\t\n582\tfn log_ack_frequency_frame<'a>(out: &mut Vec<u8>, bytes_in: &'a [u8]) -> Option<&'a [u8]> {\n583\t    let bytes_begin = bytes_in;\n584\t    let mut bytes = frames_varint_skip(bytes_in)?;\n585\t    bytes = frames_varint_skip(bytes)?;\n586\t    bytes = frames_varint_skip(bytes)?;\n587\t    bytes = frames_varint_skip(bytes)?;\n588\t    bytes = frames_varint_skip(bytes)?;\n589\t    let consumed = bytes_begin.len() - bytes.len();\n590\t    append_frame(out, &bytes_begin[..consumed]);\n591\t    Some(bytes)\n592\t}\n593\t\n594\tfn log_immediate_ack_frame<'a>(out: &mut Vec<u8>, bytes_in: &'a [u8]) -> Option<&'a [u8]> {\n595\t    let bytes_begin = bytes_in;\n596\t    let bytes = frames_varint_skip(bytes_in)?;\n597\t    let consumed = bytes_begin.len() - bytes.len();\n598\t    append_frame(out, &bytes_begin[..consumed]);\n599\t    Some(bytes)\n600\t}\n601\t\n602\tfn log_padding<'a>(out: &mut Vec<u8>, bytes_in: &'a [u8]) -> Option<&'a [u8]> {\n603\t    if bytes_in.is_empty() {\n604\t        return None;\n605\t    }\n606\t    append_frame(out, &bytes_in[..1]);\n607\t    let ftype = bytes_in[0];\n608\t    let mut idx = 0usize;\n609\t    while idx < bytes_in.len() && bytes_in[idx] == ftype {\n610\t        idx += 1;\n611\t    }\n612\t    Some(&bytes_in[idx..])\n613\t}\n614\t\n615\tfn log_bdp_frame<'a>(out: &mut Vec<u8>, bytes_in: &'a [u8]) -> Option<&'a [u8]> {\n616\t    let bytes_begin = bytes_in;\n617\t    let mut bytes = frames_varint_skip(bytes_in)?;\n618\t    bytes = frames_varint_skip(bytes)?;\n619\t    bytes = frames_varint_skip(bytes)?;\n620\t    bytes = frames_varint_skip(bytes)?;\n621\t    let (ip_len, rest) = read_length(bytes)?;\n622\t    bytes = skip_fixed(rest, ip_len)?;\n623\t    let consumed = bytes_begin.len() - bytes.len();\n624\t    append_frame(out, &bytes_begin[..consumed]);\n625\t    Some(bytes)\n626\t}\n627\t\n628\tfn log_observed_address_frame<'a>(\n629\t    out: &mut Vec<u8>,\n630\t    bytes_in: &'a [u8],\n631\t    ftype: u64,\n632\t) -> Option<&'a [u8]> {\n633\t    let bytes_begin = bytes_in;\n634\t    let ip_len = if (ftype & 1) == 0 { 4 } else { 16 };\n635\t    let data_len = ip_len + 2;\n636\t    let mut bytes = frames_varint_skip(bytes_in)?;\n637\t    bytes = frames_varint_skip(bytes)?;\n638\t    bytes = skip_fixed(bytes, data_len)?;\n639\t    let consumed = bytes_begin.len() - bytes.len();\n640\t    append_frame(out, &bytes_begin[..consumed]);\n641\t    Some(bytes)\n642\t}\n643\t\n644\tfn log_erroring_frame<'a>(out: &mut Vec<u8>, bytes_in: &'a [u8]) -> Option<&'a [u8]> {\n645\t    let copied = bytes_in.len().min(8);\n646\t    append_frame(out, &bytes_in[..copied]);\n647\t    None\n648\t}\n649\t\n650\t/// Walk a packet payload's frame stream, appending one\n651\t/// length-prefixed entry per frame to `out`.  C:\n652\t/// `picoquic_binlog_frames`.\n653\tfn binlog_frames(out: &mut Vec<u8>, mut bytes: &[u8]) {\n654\t    loop {\n655\t        if bytes.is_empty() {\n656\t            return;\n657\t        }\n658\t        let mut ftype = 0u64;\n659\t        let ftype_ll = varint_decode(bytes, &mut ftype);\n660\t        if ftype_ll == 0 {\n661\t            return;\n662\t        }\n663\t        if ftype < 64 && ftype_ll != 1 {\n664\t            return;\n665\t        }\n666\t\n667\t        if ftype >= FrameType::StreamRangeMin as u64 && ftype <= FrameType::StreamRangeMax as u64 {\n668\t            match log_stream_frame(out, bytes) {\n669\t                Some(rest) => bytes = rest,\n670\t                None => return,\n671\t            }\n672\t            continue;\n673\t        }\n674\t\n675\t        let next: Option<&[u8]> = match ftype {\n676\t            v if v == FrameType::Ack as u64\n677\t                || v == FrameType::AckEcn as u64\n678\t                || v == FrameType::PathAck as u64\n679\t                || v == FrameType::PathAckEcn as u64 =>\n680\t            {\n681\t                log_ack_frame(out, bytes)\n682\t            }\n683\t            v if v == FrameType::RetireConnectionId as u64 => {\n684\t                log_simple_n_varints(out, bytes, true, 1)\n685\t            }\n686\t            v if v == FrameType::PathRetireConnectionId as u64 => {\n687\t                log_simple_n_varints(out, bytes, false, 2)\n688\t            }\n689\t            v if v == FrameType::Padding as u64 || v == FrameType::Ping as u64 => {\n690\t                log_padding(out, bytes)\n691\t            }\n692\t            v if v == FrameType::ResetStream as u64 => log_simple_n_varints(out, bytes, true, 3),\n693\t            v if v == FrameType::ResetStreamAt as u64 => log_simple_n_varints(out, bytes, true, 4),\n694\t            v if v == FrameType::ConnectionClose as u64 => log_close_frame(out, bytes),\n695\t            v if v == FrameType::ApplicationClose as u64 => log_app_close_frame(out, bytes),\n696\t            v if v == FrameType::MaxData as u64 => log_simple_n_varints(out, bytes, true, 1),\n697\t            v if v == FrameType::MaxStreamData as u64 => log_simple_n_varints(out, bytes, true, 2),\n698\t            v if v == FrameType::MaxStreamsBidir as u64\n699\t                || v == FrameType::MaxStreamsUnidir as u64 =>\n700\t            {\n701\t                log_simple_n_varints(out, bytes, true, 1)\n702\t            }\n703\t            v if v == FrameType::DataBlocked as u64 => log_simple_n_varints(out, bytes, true, 1),\n704\t            v if v == FrameType::StreamDataBlocked as u64 => {\n705\t                log_simple_n_varints(out, bytes, true, 2)\n706\t            }\n707\t            v if v == FrameType::StreamsBlockedBidir as u64\n708\t                || v == FrameType::StreamsBlockedUnidir as u64 =>\n709\t            {\n710\t                log_simple_n_varints(out, bytes, true, 1)\n711\t            }\n712\t            v if v == FrameType::NewConnectionId as u64 => log_new_connection_id_frame(out, bytes),\n713\t            v if v == FrameType::PathNewConnectionId as u64 => {\n714\t                log_path_new_connection_id_frame(out, bytes)\n715\t            }\n716\t            v if v == FrameType::StopSending as u64 => log_simple_n_varints(out, bytes, true, 2),\n717\t            v if v == FrameType::PathChallenge as u64 || v == FrameType::PathResponse as u64 => {\n718\t                log_path_frame(out, bytes)\n719\t            }\n720\t            v if v == FrameType::CryptoHs as u64 => log_crypto_hs_frame(out, bytes),\n721\t            v if v == FrameType::NewToken as u64 => log_new_token_frame(out, bytes),\n722\t            v if v == FrameType::HandshakeDone as u64 => log_handshake_done_frame(out, bytes),\n723\t            v if v == FrameType::Datagram as u64 || v == FrameType::DatagramL as u64 => {\n724\t                log_datagram_frame(out, bytes)\n725\t            }\n726\t            v if v == FrameType::AckFrequency as u64 => log_ack_frequency_frame(out, bytes),\n727\t            v if v == FrameType::ImmediateAck as u64 => log_immediate_ack_frame(out, bytes),\n728\t            v if v == FrameType::TimeStamp as u64 => log_time_stamp_frame(out, bytes),\n729\t            v if v == FrameType::PathAbandon as u64 => log_path_abandon_frame(out, bytes),\n730\t            v if v == FrameType::PathBackup as u64 || v == FrameType::PathAvailable as u64 => {\n731\t                log_path_available_or_backup_frame(out, bytes)\n732\t            }\n733\t            v if v == FrameType::Bdp as u64 => log_bdp_frame(out, bytes),\n734\t            v if v == FrameType::ObservedAddressV4 as u64\n735\t                || v == FrameType::ObservedAddressV6 as u64 =>\n736\t            {\n737\t                log_observed_address_frame(out, bytes, ftype)\n738\t            }\n739\t            _ => log_erroring_frame(out, bytes),\n740\t        };\n741\t\n742\t        match next {\n743\t            Some(rest) => bytes = rest,\n744\t            None => return,\n745\t        }\n746\t    }\n747\t}\n748\t\n749\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n750\t// Low-level per-event writers.\n751\t//\n752\t// Free functions on a [`File`] sink — these don't carry a `Connection`\n753\t// handle, so calls are namespaced through the module path\n754\t// (`binlog::pdu(...)`, `binlog::packet(...)`,\n755\t// `binlog::tls_ticket(...)`).  Callers usually go through the\n756\t// [`Connection`] methods below, which thread through `connection.f_binlog`; the\n757\t// file-only writers are kept public for the contexts where the\n758\t// caller already owns the handle (e.g., the binlog backend's\n759\t// implementation of [`crate::logger::Logger`]).\n760\t\n761\t/// Write a PDU arrival/departure record to `f`.\n762\t///\n763\t/// C: `void binlog_pdu(FILE*, const ConnectionId*, int,\n764\t/// uint64_t, const struct sockaddr*, const struct sockaddr*, size_t,\n765\t/// uint64_t, unsigned char)`.\n766\tpub fn pdu(\n767\t    f: &mut File,\n768\t    cid: &ConnectionId,\n769\t    receiving: bool,\n770\t    current_time: Instant,\n771\t    addr_peer: &SocketAddr,\n772\t    addr_local: &SocketAddr,\n773\t    packet_length: usize,\n774\t    unique_path_id: u64,\n775\t    ecn: u8,\n776\t) {\n777\t    let mut buf = ByteStreamBuf::default();\n778\t    let Some(mut msg) = buf.stream(BYTESTREAM_MAX_BUFFER_SIZE) else {\n779\t        return;\n780\t    };\n781\t\n782\t    let event = if receiving {\n783\t        LogEventType::PduRecv\n784\t    } else {\n785\t        LogEventType::PduSent\n786\t    };\n787\t    compose_event_header(&mut msg, cid, current_time, 0, event);\n788\t\n789\t    let _ = msg.write_addr(addr_peer);\n790\t    let _ = msg.write_varint(packet_length as u64);\n791\t    let _ = msg.write_addr(addr_local);\n792\t    let _ = msg.write_varint(unique_path_id);\n793\t    let _ = msg.write_u8(ecn);\n794\t\n795\t    let payload: Vec<u8> = msg.as_bytes().to_vec();\n796\t    drop(msg);\n797\t    write_record(f, &payload);\n798\t}\n799\t\n800\t/// Write a decrypted-packet record to `f`.  Binary alternative to\n801\t/// `log_decrypted_segment()`.\n802\t///\n803\t/// C: `void binlog_packet(FILE*, const ConnectionId*,\n804\t/// uint64_t, int, uint64_t, const packet_header*,\n805\t/// const uint8_t*, size_t)`.\n806\tpub fn packet(\n807\t    f: &mut File,\n808\t    cid: &ConnectionId,\n809\t    path_id: u64,\n810\t    receiving: bool,\n811\t    current_time: Instant,\n812\t    ph: &PacketHeader,\n813\t    bytes: &[u8],\n814\t) {\n815\t    // Buffer the whole record (header + framing) into a `Vec<u8>`,\n816\t    // then write 4-byte length + payload.  The C version reserves\n817\t    // four bytes via `fseek`/`ftell` because `picoquic_binlog_frames`\n818\t    // writes straight to the FILE; the buffered shape is the\n819\t    // natural Rust equivalent.\n820\t    let mut payload: Vec<u8> = Vec::new();\n821\t\n822\t    {\n823\t        let mut buf = ByteStreamBuf::default();\n824\t        let Some(mut msg) = buf.stream(BYTESTREAM_MAX_BUFFER_SIZE) else {\n825\t            return;\n826\t        };\n827\t\n828\t        let event = if receiving {\n829\t            LogEventType::PacketRecv\n830\t        } else {\n831\t            LogEventType::PacketSent\n832\t        };\n833\t        compose_event_header(&mut msg, cid, current_time, path_id, event);\n834\t\n835\t        let _ = msg.write_varint(bytes.len() as u64);\n836\t\n837\t        // Packed header byte: quic_bit_is_zero<<6 | spin<<1 | key_phase.\n838\t        let flags: u8 = (if ph.quic_bit_is_zero { 64 } else { 0 })\n839\t            + (if ph.spin { 2 } else { 0 })\n840\t            + (if ph.key_phase { 1 } else { 0 });\n841\t        let _ = msg.write_u8(flags);\n842\t        let _ = msg.write_varint(ph.payload_length as u64);\n843\t        let _ = msg.write_varint(ph.packet_type as u64);\n844\t        let _ = msg.write_varint(ph.packet_number_full);\n845\t\n846\t        let _ = msg.write_cid(&ph.dest_connection_id);\n847\t        let _ = msg.write_cid(&ph.src_connection_id);\n848\t\n849\t        if ph.packet_type != PacketType::OneRttProtected\n850\t            && ph.packet_type != PacketType::VersionNegotiation\n851\t        {\n852\t            let _ = msg.write_u32(ph.version);\n853\t        }\n854\t\n855\t        if ph.packet_type == PacketType::Initial {\n856\t            let _ = msg.write_varint(ph.token_bytes.len() as u64);\n857\t            let _ = msg.write_bytes(&ph.token_bytes);\n858\t        }\n859\t\n860\t        payload.extend_from_slice(msg.as_bytes());\n861\t    }\n862\t\n863\t    if ph.packet_type == PacketType::VersionNegotiation || ph.packet_type == PacketType::Retry {\n864\t        let payload_slice = bytes.get(ph.offset..).unwrap_or(&[]);\n865\t        append_frame(&mut payload, payload_slice);\n866\t    } else if ph.packet_type != PacketType::Error {\n867\t        let end = ph.offset.saturating_add(ph.payload_length).min(bytes.len());\n868\t        let frames_slice = bytes.get(ph.offset..end).unwrap_or(&[]);\n869\t        binlog_frames(&mut payload, frames_slice);\n870\t    }\n871\t\n872\t    write_record(f, &payload);\n873\t}\n874\t\n875\t/// Write a TLS session-ticket record to `f`.  Binary alternative\n876\t/// to `log_tls_ticket()`.  The connection-id parameter is `Copy`\n877\t/// and passed by value to mirror the C ABI.\n878\t///\n879\t/// C: `void binlog_picotls_ticket(FILE*, ConnectionId,\n880\t/// uint8_t*, uint16_t)`.\n881\tpub fn tls_ticket(f: &mut File, cnx_id: ConnectionId, ticket: &[u8]) {\n882\t    let mut buf = ByteStreamBuf::default();\n883\t    let Some(mut msg) = buf.stream(BYTESTREAM_MAX_BUFFER_SIZE) else {\n884\t        return;\n885\t    };\n886\t    compose_event_header(\n887\t        &mut msg,\n888\t        &cnx_id,\n889\t        Instant::from_ticks(0),\n890\t        0,\n891\t        LogEventType::TlsKeyUpdate,\n892\t    );\n893\t    let _ = msg.write_varint(ticket.len() as u64);\n894\t    let _ = msg.write_bytes(ticket);\n895\t\n896\t    let payload = msg.as_bytes().to_vec();\n897\t    drop(msg);\n898\t    write_record(f, &payload);\n899\t}\n900\t\n901\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n902\t// High-level per-event writers — methods on [`Connection`].\n903\t//\n904\t// Each method pulls the file handle from `connection.f_binlog` and\n905\t// delegates to one of the low-level writers above (or composes\n906\t// several records).  Bundling them as a [`Binlog`] trait (rather\n907\t// than inherent methods on `Connection`) lets callers opt into the\n908\t// capability with `use crate::binlog::Binlog`, scopes the names to\n909\t// the trait, and keeps the names short — no `binlog_` prefix\n910\t// needed since the trait disambiguates.\n911\t\n912\t/// Binary trace recording for a [`Connection`].  Each method writes\n913\t/// one record (or composes a few records) into the connection's\n914\t/// `f_binlog` file; bringing the trait into scope opts the caller\n915\t/// into the capability.  C: the per-event writers in\n916\t/// `quic/binlog.c`.\n917\tpub trait Binlog {\n918\t    /// Report that a packet was dropped due to some error.\n919\t    ///\n920\t    /// C: `void binlog_dropped_packet(Connection*, Path*,\n921\t    /// packet_header*, size_t, int, uint64_t)`.\n922\t    fn dropped_packet(\n923\t        &mut self,\n924\t        path_x: &mut Path,\n925\t        ph: &PacketHeader,\n926\t        packet_size: usize,\n927\t        err: i32,\n928\t        current_time: Instant,\n929\t    );\n930\t\n931\t    /// Report that a packet was buffered waiting for decryption.\n932\t    ///\n933\t    /// C: `void binlog_buffered_packet(Connection*, Path*,\n934\t    /// packet_type_enum, uint64_t)`.\n935\t    fn buffered_packet(&mut self, path_x: &mut Path, ptype: PacketType, current_time: Instant);\n936\t\n937\t    /// Binary alternative to `log_outgoing_segment()`.  `bytes`\n938\t    /// is the unencrypted payload (the C `length` parameter is\n939\t    /// folded into the slice); `send_buffer` is the encrypted,\n940\t    /// padded wire form.  `pn_length` is the offset of the\n941\t    /// packet-number field inside `bytes`.\n942\t    ///\n943\t    /// C: `void binlog_outgoing_packet(Connection*, Path*,\n944\t    /// uint8_t*, uint64_t, size_t, size_t, uint8_t*, size_t,\n945\t    /// uint64_t)`.\n946\t    fn outgoing_packet(\n947\t        &mut self,\n948\t        path_x: &mut Path,\n949\t        bytes: &[u8],\n950\t        sequence_number: u64,\n951\t        pn_length: usize,\n952\t        send_buffer: &[u8],\n953\t        current_time: Instant,\n954\t    );\n955\t\n956\t    /// Log a packet-lost event.  `dcid` is `None` when the remote\n957\t    /// connection ID is unknown — the C body emits a single zero\n958\t    /// byte in that case.\n959\t    ///\n960\t    /// C: `void binlog_packet_lost(Connection*, Path*,\n961\t    /// packet_type_enum, uint64_t, char const*,\n962\t    /// ConnectionId*, size_t, uint64_t)`.\n963\t    fn packet_lost(\n964\t        &mut self,\n965\t        path_x: &mut Path,\n966\t        ptype: PacketType,\n967\t        sequence_number: u64,\n968\t        trigger: &str,\n969\t        dcid: Option<&ConnectionId>,\n970\t        packet_size: usize,\n971\t        current_time: Instant,\n972\t    );\n973\t\n974\t    /// Log negotiated SNI / ALPN.  Empty `sni`/`alpn` slices stand\n975\t    /// in for the C `(NULL, 0)` callers.\n976\t    ///\n977\t    /// C: `void binlog_negotiated_alpn(Connection*, int,\n978\t    /// uint8_t const*, size_t, uint8_t const*, size_t,\n979\t    /// const PtlsIovec*, size_t)`.\n980\t    fn negotiated_alpn(&mut self, is_local: bool, sni: &[u8], alpn: &[u8], alpn_list: &[&[u8]]);\n981\t\n982\t    /// Binary alternative to `log_transport_extension()`.\n983\t    ///\n984\t    /// C: `void binlog_transport_extension(Connection*, int, size_t,\n985\t    /// uint8_t*)`.\n986\t    fn transport_extension(&mut self, is_local: bool, params: &[u8]);\n987\t\n988\t    /// Open the per-connection binlog file and emit the\n989\t    /// `new_connection` record.  Idempotent — the C body is a no-op\n990\t    /// when neither `quic->binlog_dir` nor `quic->qlog_dir` are\n991\t    /// set, or when `quic->bin_log_fns` is `NULL`.\n992\t    ///\n993\t    /// C: `void binlog_new_connection(Connection*)`.\n994\t    fn new_connection(&mut self);\n995\t\n996\t    /// Emit the `connection_close` record and close the\n997\t    /// per-connection binlog file.  Safe to call when no binlog is\n998\t    /// currently open (the C body guards on `connection->f_binlog !=\n999\t    /// NULL`).\n1000\t    ///\n1001\t    /// C: `void binlog_close_connection(Connection*)`.\n1002\t    fn close_connection(&mut self);\n1003\t\n1004\t    /// Log the state of the congestion controller, retransmission\n1005\t    /// queues, etc.  Called either just after processing an\n1006\t    /// incoming packet or just after sending one.\n1007\t    ///\n1008\t    /// C: `void binlog_cc_dump(Connection*, Path*, uint64_t)`.\n1009\t    fn cc_dump(&mut self, path_x: &mut Path, current_time: Instant);\n1010\t}\n1011\t\n1012\timpl Binlog for Connection {\n1013\t    fn dropped_packet(\n1014\t        &mut self,\n1015\t        path_x: &mut Path,\n1016\t        ph: &PacketHeader,\n1017\t        packet_size: usize,\n1018\t        err: i32,\n1019\t        current_time: Instant,\n1020\t    ) {\n1021\t        if self.f_binlog.is_none() {\n1022\t            return;\n1023\t        }\n1024\t        let cid = self.initial_connection_id;\n1025\t        let path_id = get_path_id(self, path_x);\n1026\t\n1027\t        let mut buf = ByteStreamBuf::default();\n1028\t        let Some(mut msg) = buf.stream(BYTESTREAM_MAX_BUFFER_SIZE) else {\n1029\t            return;\n1030\t        };\n1031\t        // Reserve four bytes for the chunk size; patch afterwards\n1032\t        // — mirrors the C source.\n1033\t        let _ = msg.write_u32(0);\n1034\t        compose_event_header(\n1035\t            &mut msg,\n1036\t            &cid,\n1037\t            current_time,\n1038\t            path_id,\n1039\t            LogEventType::PacketDropped,\n1040\t        );\n1041\t        let _ = msg.write_varint(ph.packet_type as u64);\n1042\t        let _ = msg.write_varint(packet_size as u64);\n1043\t        let _ = msg.write_varint(err as u64);\n1044\t\n1045\t        let body_len = (msg.len().saturating_sub(4)) as u32;\n1046\t        let mut payload = msg.as_bytes().to_vec();\n1047\t        drop(msg);\n1048\t        payload[..4].copy_from_slice(&body_len.to_be_bytes());\n1049\t\n1050\t        if let Some(f) = self.f_binlog.as_mut() {\n1051\t            let _ = f.write_all(&payload);\n1052\t        }\n1053\t    }\n1054\t\n1055\t    fn buffered_packet(&mut self, path_x: &mut Path, ptype: PacketType, current_time: Instant) {\n1056\t        if self.f_binlog.is_none() {\n1057\t            return;\n1058\t        }\n1059\t        let cid = self.initial_connection_id;\n1060\t        let path_id = get_path_id(self, path_x);\n1061\t\n1062\t        let mut buf = ByteStreamBuf::default();\n1063\t        let Some(mut msg) = buf.stream(BYTESTREAM_MAX_BUFFER_SIZE) else {\n1064\t            return;\n1065\t        };\n1066\t        let _ = msg.write_u32(0);\n1067\t        compose_event_header(\n1068\t            &mut msg,\n1069\t            &cid,\n1070\t            current_time,\n1071\t            path_id,\n1072\t            LogEventType::PacketBuffered,\n1073\t        );\n1074\t        let _ = msg.write_varint(ptype as u64);\n1075\t        let _ = msg.write_str(\"keys_unavailable\");\n1076\t\n1077\t        let body_len = (msg.len().saturating_sub(4)) as u32;\n1078\t        let mut payload = msg.as_bytes().to_vec();\n1079\t        drop(msg);\n1080\t        payload[..4].copy_from_slice(&body_len.to_be_bytes());\n1081\t        if let Some(f) = self.f_binlog.as_mut() {\n1082\t            let _ = f.write_all(&payload);\n1083\t        }\n1084\t    }\n1085\t\n1086\t    fn outgoing_packet(\n1087\t        &mut self,\n1088\t        path_x: &mut Path,\n1089\t        bytes: &[u8],\n1090\t        sequence_number: u64,\n1091\t        pn_length: usize,\n1092\t        send_buffer: &[u8],\n1093\t        current_time: Instant,\n1094\t    ) {\n1095\t        if self.f_binlog.is_none() {\n1096\t            return;\n1097\t        }\n1098\t        let cid = self.initial_connection_id;\n1099\t        let path_id = get_path_id(self, path_x);\n1100\t\n1101\t        // The C body calls `picoquic_parse_packet_header(cnx->quic,\n1102\t        // send_buffer, …)` to recover the header from the encrypted\n1103\t        // wire form.  `parse_packet_header` lives on [`Quic`] and\n1104\t        // `Connection` carries no back-pointer; do a minimal in-line\n1105\t        // parse so we can still emit a useful record.\n1106\t        let mut ph = parse_outgoing_header(send_buffer);\n1107\t\n1108\t        let checksum_length: usize = {\n1109\t            let epoch = match ph.packet_type {\n1110\t                PacketType::OneRttProtected => crate::internal::Epoch::OneRtt,\n1111\t                PacketType::ZeroRttProtected => crate::internal::Epoch::ZeroRtt,\n1112\t                PacketType::Handshake => crate::internal::Epoch::Handshake,\n1113\t                _ => crate::internal::Epoch::Initial,\n1114\t            };\n1115\t            if self.crypto_context[epoch as usize].aead_encrypt.is_some() {\n1116\t                self.get_checksum_length(epoch)\n1117\t            } else {\n1118\t                16\n1119\t            }\n1120\t        };\n1121\t\n1122\t        ph.packet_number_full = sequence_number;\n1123\t        ph.packet_number_truncated = sequence_number as u32;\n1124\t        if ph.packet_type != PacketType::Retry && ph.packet_number_offset != 0 {\n1125\t            ph.offset = ph.packet_number_offset + pn_length;\n1126\t            ph.payload_length = ph.payload_length.saturating_sub(pn_length);\n1127\t        }\n1128\t        if ph.packet_type != PacketType::VersionNegotiation {\n1129\t            if ph.payload_length > checksum_length {\n1130\t                ph.payload_length -= checksum_length;\n1131\t            } else {\n1132\t                ph.payload_length = 0;\n1133\t            }\n1134\t        }\n1135\t\n1136\t        if let Some(f) = self.f_binlog.as_mut() {\n1137\t            packet(f, &cid, path_id, false, current_time, &ph, bytes);\n1138\t        }\n1139\t    }\n1140\t\n1141\t    fn packet_lost(\n1142\t        &mut self,\n1143\t        path_x: &mut Path,\n1144\t        ptype: PacketType,\n1145\t        sequence_number: u64,\n1146\t        trigger: &str,\n1147\t        dcid: Option<&ConnectionId>,\n1148\t        packet_size: usize,\n1149\t        current_time: Instant,\n1150\t    ) {\n1151\t        if self.f_binlog.is_none() {\n1152\t            return;\n1153\t        }\n1154\t        let cid = self.initial_connection_id;\n1155\t        let path_id = get_path_id(self, path_x);\n1156\t\n1157\t        let mut buf = ByteStreamBuf::default();\n1158\t        let Some(mut msg) = buf.stream(BYTESTREAM_MAX_BUFFER_SIZE) else {\n1159\t            return;\n1160\t        };\n1161\t        let _ = msg.write_u32(0);\n1162\t        compose_event_header(\n1163\t            &mut msg,\n1164\t            &cid,\n1165\t            current_time,\n1166\t            path_id,\n1167\t            LogEventType::PacketLost,\n1168\t        );\n1169\t        let _ = msg.write_varint(ptype as u64);\n1170\t        let _ = msg.write_varint(sequence_number);\n1171\t        let _ = msg.write_str(trigger);\n1172\t        match dcid {\n1173\t         